Error: Jet.ScopeMemberArgumentMismatch: `.expect_fail` takes an optional runtime stop name and `message: "text"`
  --> Tests/UI/scope_expect_fail_empty_message.jet:2:17
    |
  2 |     .expect_fail(message: "") {
    |                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: The name is a registered runtime stop; the message is a non-empty string literal matched as a case-sensitive substring
 Fix: Write `.expect_fail { … }`, `.expect_fail(Jet.ArithmeticOrBoundsFailure) { … }`, or `.expect_fail(Jet.Panic, message: "reason") { … }`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ScopeMemberArgumentMismatch
